    # c15.s01
    scene bg c15_harbour_sunset
    with fade
    "He knew which cradle. It was the last in the row, the one with the square name cut beside it."
    "He turned in the water. Sefa's arms were still round his chest, holding him up, and she cried out at him to be still."

    scene cg c15_dragon_ribs
    with dissolve
    "The Dragon lay across the mouth of the harbour where he had left it. Its ribs stood out of the swell in a long line against the sunset, each with its mane of bright water."

    scene bg c15_harbour_sunset
    with dissolve
    "He had ridden on its brow that morning and been a kilometre long. He reached for it now as he would have reached for his own hand."
    "Someone else had hold of it."
    "It was not like the fight in the gallery. There was no blow. There was only a pressure, steady and patient, like a man leaning his weight on the other side of a door."
    "Ilan knew every wheel in that heart. He had laid them out on the floor in order and put them back with his own hands. But the other had ridden the Dragon before Okonta was born."
    "He had lain in its gallery as a young man, and listened to it, year after year, with the best head of the sixty. He could not have mended a hinge on it. He knew it as a blind man knows a house."
    "The Dragon's note wavered. The great blunt head swung in toward the harbour, toward Ilan, and stopped. The bound water flared white along its whole length. He heard the ribs groan."
    "{i}Stay,{/i} he asked it. {i}Please. Stay.{/i}"
    "It was all he had. He was ebbed to the bone, and shaking, and the Thread wanted attention as a needle wants it. He had none left to give. He held the door with his fingertips."
    "Above the city, the big screens changed."
    "They showed a crest he had seen on a building with no windows. A voice spoke out of every wall in Port Halcyon. It was speaking, in that moment, out of every wall on every island."
    "It was a calm voice, and unhurried, and Ilan had heard it across a table once a year since he was sixteen."
    "It said that in view of the extraordinary situation, Meridian Assurance was exercising its rights under all outstanding instruments. Every debt was called. Citizens, houses, cities and corporations had thirty days to pay, in scrip or in service."
    "It said that service would be accepted at any Meridian door. And it said that in consideration of that service, the house would issue to every household that gave it a deed of ground."
    "The ground was new. It would be made available within the season. There would be enough."

    show p sefa_afraid as right at head_right
    with qd
    c_sefa "What does that mean?"

    hide right
    with qd
    "He could not answer her. The door was going."
    "Okonta had seen the Dragon's head swing. She did not ask what it meant. She went for the cradles with fifteen needles behind her, in a silver line, low over the water."
    "They never reached them. Grey needles came out of the smoke round the eastern head, where forty warships lay canted in their berths. There were twenty of them and more."
    "They had been waiting there all afternoon, behind the fleet. They met the silver line over the harbour mouth, in the last of the light, and every camera Orrin owned was pointing at it."

