    "It did not open. {i}He tells it who to let in,{/i} a boy had said in a dark hall, a long time ago. She beat on it with her fist."

    scene bg c15_harbour_sunset
    with dissolve
    "He did not let go. He was sure of that afterwards. There was simply nothing left to hold with."
    "The Dragon turned its head to the open sea."
    "It went out past the breakwater along the white road it had come by. He felt it run west. He felt it for a hundred kilometres, and two hundred, a long bright hum going away. Then it tilted, and went down."

